      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 8.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Let me think, um, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.85,
      "end_seconds": 14.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "not at all, please sit what seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.76,
      "end_seconds": 29.99,
      "duration_seconds": 14.23,
      "text": "Good morning, um, doctor. I came along to help out. It's crushing chest pain, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.57,
      "end_seconds": 34.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Right, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.39,
      "end_seconds": 39.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "About about a month, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 41.17,
      "end_seconds": 45.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like about two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.88,
      "end_seconds": 51.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.01,
      "end_seconds": 54.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "yeah, roughly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.71,
      "end_seconds": 84.36,
      "duration_seconds": 16.65,
      "text": "Exertion definitely sets it off. I'd give it a five, um, out of ten. I did have pain going into my left arm at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.41,
      "end_seconds": 89.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Alright, any cough, fever or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.2,
      "end_seconds": 96.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "no cough, fever or leg swelling, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.48,
      "end_seconds": 100.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.17,
      "end_seconds": 107.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "nothing on the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.74,
      "end_seconds": 111.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.11,
      "end_seconds": 116.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.0,
      "end_seconds": 121.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.61,
      "end_seconds": 126.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "my son has asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.32,
      "end_seconds": 136.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.25,
      "end_seconds": 139.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "no, nothing at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.5,
      "end_seconds": 144.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Any regular medication, tablets or creams?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.74,
      "end_seconds": 149.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Mm, no, I'm not on anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.66,
      "end_seconds": 172.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.06,
      "end_seconds": 184.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. No, I share a house with my brother. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.71,
      "end_seconds": 192.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.91,
      "end_seconds": 197.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.19,
      "end_seconds": 203.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.93,
      "end_seconds": 218.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.11,
      "end_seconds": 239.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, heart rate 116, respiratory rate 17, temperature is 36.6 degrees, BP is 122 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.98,
      "end_seconds": 242.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.89,
      "end_seconds": 246.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.77,
      "end_seconds": 272.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.23,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: It points towards a possible heart attack. We shouldn't forget unstable angina."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.3,
      "end_seconds": 295.76,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "I'm sending you for a troponin blood test because of chest pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.25,
      "end_seconds": 303.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.23,
      "end_seconds": 323.03,
      "duration_seconds": 18.8,
      "text": "I'll start you on aspirin, 300 milligrams, once now, single dose that's for possible heart attack the pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up stay lying down and do not eat or drink that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.94,
      "end_seconds": 326.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}